{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReverseCascade","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReverseCascade","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReverseRow"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_insert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_insert","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseCascade.lean#L126-L155","doc":"**The cascade inversion law.** Undoing `insert T x` at the row where it put its new cell\nrecovers `T` and reports `x`.\n\nThe recursion follows `insert`'s own: at the appending row, brick 1's no-bump case says the row is\n`old ++ [x]`, so `dropLast` / `getLast?` recover it; at a bumping row, brick 1's inversion law\n(`rowUninsert_rowInsert`) undoes the bump and the recursion supplies the value to push up. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_succ","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseCascade.lean#L117-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_zero","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseCascade.lean#L114-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_nil","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseCascade.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseCascade.lean#L96-L110","doc":"**The reverse cascade.** `uninsert T i` removes the last cell of row `i` and pushes the removed\nvalue up through rows `i-1, …, 0` by reverse row insertion, returning the value displaced out of\nthe top row.\n\nAt the target row a length-one row is deleted rather than left empty — see `NoEmptyRows`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_noEmptyRows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_noEmptyRows","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseCascade.lean#L66-L94","doc":"`insert` never creates an empty row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_eq_append_of_none","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_eq_append_of_none","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseCascade.lean#L53-L64","doc":"**A no-bump insertion appends.** When `rowInsert` reports no bump it has put `x` at the end. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.noEmptyRows_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.noEmptyRows_nil","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseCascade.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.NoEmptyRows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.NoEmptyRows","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseCascade.lean#L47-L49","doc":"**No empty rows** — a tableau well-formedness condition. `uninsert` needs it to know that a row\nlosing its only cell should be deleted rather than left behind as `[]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.newRowIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.newRowIndex","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReverseCascade.lean#L38-L45","doc":"**Where the new cell lands.** `insert T x` appends a cell to exactly one row; this records its\nindex, by the same recursion `insert` itself uses. ","signatureChunk":0}]}